    "1/1": "Based on the VoiceOver/JAWS output you showed, the React version is putting an `aria-label` on the `<label>` element itself, which actually prevents the inner text from being announced. In the vanilla HTML we rely on the native `<label for=\"\u2026\">Label text</label>` association, which works correctly in all AT \u2014 the screen reader simply reads the visible text.\n\nIn our React `<RadioButton>` we should:\n\n- Remove the `aria-label={labelText}` from the `<label>` entirely.\n- Let the native label/text association carry the accessible name.\n- We don\u2019t need to add an `aria-label` anywhere else \u2014 if you are hiding the visual label with `hideLabel`, it still lives in the DOM (with a visually-hidden class) and will be announced.\n\nHere is a one-file patch to remove the stray `aria-label` on the `<label>`.\n\n```javascript\n### packages/react/src/components/RadioButton/RadioButton.js\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n        <label\n          htmlFor={this.uid}\n          className={`${prefix}--radio-button__label`}\n          aria-label={labelText}>\n          <span className={`${prefix}--radio-button__appearance`} />\n          <span className={innerLabelClasses}>{labelText}</span>\n        </label>\n=======\n        <label\n          htmlFor={this.uid}\n          className={`${prefix}--radio-button__label`}>\n          <span className={`${prefix}--radio-button__appearance`} />\n          <span className={innerLabelClasses}>{labelText}</span>\n        </label>\n>>>>>>> REPLACE\n```\n\nAfter this change your rendered DOM will be:\n\n```html\n<div class=\"bx--radio-button-wrapper\">\n  <input id=\"radio-1\" name=\"radio-button-group\" type=\"radio\" class=\"bx--radio-button\" value=\"standard\" />\n  <label for=\"radio-1\" class=\"bx--radio-button__label\">\n    <span class=\"bx--radio-button__appearance\"></span>\n    <span class=\"bx--visually-hidden\">Radio button label</span>\n  </label>\n</div>\n```\n\nWhich restores the proper native label association and VoiceOver/JAWS will once again announce \u201cRadio button label.\u201d"
